ege-football/story/_/id/47594926/minnesota-transfer-safety-koi-perich-commits-oregon-ducks-football","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas, Penn St. players lead AP preseason All-America 1st team","description":"Texas edge rusher Colin Simmons is among three Longhorns on The Associated Press All-America team. No. 2 Penn State also had three players, giving the Nittany Lions and Longhorns the most on the team.","published":"2025-08-18T20:05:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/46008870/texas-penn-st-players-lead-ap-preseason-all-america-1st-team","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Anger Index: Why Texas Tech, Tennessee and the Group of 6 should be mad","description":"Ranking the teams who should be most upset about their latest CFP ranking.","published":"2026-11-18T04:25:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510905/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-texas-tech","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Michigan to hire Texas A&M's Trev Alberts as athletic director","description":"Michigan has reached a deal to hire Texas A&M athletic director Trev Alberts to replace the departing Warde Manuel, sources told ESPN on Tuesday.","published":"2026-11-18T05:46:35.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50516550/michigan-hire-texas-trev-alberts-athletic-director","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on College Football Playoff bubble after the committee's third ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-18T03:42:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's third top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's third set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:34:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514170/cfp-2026-third-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest surges into CFP top 12; top 4 unchanged while Texas jumps Notre Dame","description":"Alabama stayed at No. 3 despite some struggles on Saturday while two-loss Texas jumped one-loss Notre Dame for No. 5 in the CFP's latest rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:55:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50515993/wake-forest-surges-cfp-top-12-texas-jumps-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pawn shop fighting 'Gold Digger' trademark filed by Jordon Hudson's company","description":"A California pawn shop is opposing a trademark application for \"Gold Digger\" filed by a company connected to Jordan Hudson, then-companion of Bill Belichick.","published":"2026-11-18T00:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50514442/pawn-shop-fights-gold-digger-trademark-filed-hudson","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Anthony Olivieri","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5142588/koi-perich","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koi_Perich"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Koi Perich","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koi_Perich","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:35:51Z","intro":"Koi Perich (born September 26, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Oregon Ducks. He previously played for the Minnesota Golden Gophers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Perich attended Esko High School in Esko, Minnesota. As a junior, he rushed for over 800 yards, notched 75 tackles, two sacks, three interceptions, four forced fumbles, and 25 touchdowns. In the first game of his senior season, Perich intercepted two passes which he returned both for touchdowns. As a senior, he amassed 27 total touchdowns: 16 rushing, five defensive, four return, one passing, and one receiving. Perich also notched 76 tackles, three interceptions, and four fumble recoveries on defense, earning all-state recognition. He accepted an invite to play in the All-American Bowl, where he intercepted a pass on the goal line and blocked a punt en route to earning game MVP honors.\n\nRECRUITING\nPerich received offers from schools such as USC, Michigan, Wisconsin, Minnesota, Iowa and Washington, as well as late offers from Florida State and Ohio State. He committed to play college football for the Minnesota Golden Gophers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman, Perich recorded 24 solo tackles, one pass defended, one forced fumble, and five interceptions. He was named first-team All-Big Ten Conference and second-team All-American following the conclusion of the regular season.\nKoi Perich entered his sophomore season in 2025 with increased responsibilities across defense, special teams, and occasional offensive snaps. Mistakes early in the season led to a reduction of offensive snaps, but Perich scored a game winning touchdown on his first career defensive score to win the schools 2025 homecoming game against Purdue.\nOn January 1, 2026, Perich announced that he would enter the transfer portal.\nOn January 12, 2026, Perich announced that he would be transferring to the University of Oregon."}]}}